<Base title="About" description="Who writes Seoul Settled, and how these guides are checked.">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>Hi, I'm Jun — I live in Seoul and write Seoul Settled to answer the questions I kept running
    into, and kept seeing other foreigners ask, about the practical side of living here: getting your
    ARC, opening a bank account, choosing jeonse vs wolse, sorting your trash correctly on the first try.</p>

    <p>Most "how to move to Korea" content online is either outdated, written for tourists instead of
    residents, or vague enough that you still have to call the government office yourself to confirm the
    real answer. Every guide here is checked against official government sources — Hi Korea, the Ministry
    of Justice, NHIS and similar — and written the way I'd explain it to a friend who just landed: step by
    step, with the specific numbers, forms and gotchas that actually trip people up.</p>

    <h2>What this site covers</h2>
    <p>Visas and residency (ARC, address reporting), banking and money, housing, health insurance and
    healthcare access, transit and apps, and the small daily-life things nobody explains before you arrive.</p>

    <h2>A note on accuracy</h2>
    <p>Immigration and insurance rules change. Every guide links to the official source it is based on so
    you can double-check the current rule yourself. Don't treat any single blog — including this one — as a
    replacement for checking the government page directly before a deadline-sensitive decision.</p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>Found something outdated, or have a topic you want covered? Say so on the relevant guide and I'll
    look into it.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
